<h2>India's top groundnut kernel destination</h2>
<p>Indonesia stands out clearly in the trade data as India's largest groundnut kernel market by a significant margin, reflecting the scale of Indonesia's food-processing sector and India's competitive position on price and available volume. Dried red chilli, dehydrated onion and guar gum round out the leading lines.</p>

<h2>Halal certification is central to this market</h2>
<p>Indonesia operates one of the world's most formalised halal certification systems, administered through BPJPH, and it's a live consideration for most food imports serving the domestic market. We arrange documentation to match whatever certifying body your importer specifies — this is worth raising at the enquiry stage rather than after a shipment is packed.</p>

<h2>BPOM registration takes lead time</h2>
<p>Food products generally need registration with BPOM, Indonesia's food and drug regulator, before import. This is typically the importer's process, but it depends on product documentation and specifications from our side — start the conversation early on a first order for a given product.</p>

